---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Quickstart - uiforagents">
  <div class="page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Quickstart</h1>
      <p>The kit is copy-in vanilla HTML/CSS/JS: no framework requirement, no build step, no runtime
      dependencies. Start from the registry, not a docs search.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="quickstart-grid">
      <section class="quickstart-col">
        <h2>For agents</h2>
        <p>Point your agent at the published surfaces; they mirror the kit package one-to-one.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a> - one line per component: description, closed variant table, behavior. Enough to pick without opening files.</li>
          <li><a href="/schema/registry.schema.json"><code>registry.schema.json</code></a> - the manifest contract every item validates against.</li>
          <li><a href="/docs/components/button.md"><code>docs/components/&lt;name&gt;.md</code></a> - generated docs twins with markup, tokens read, and validation steps.</li>
          <li><a href="/items/button/button.html"><code>items/&lt;name&gt;/</code></a> - the item sources the index lines reference: markup, CSS, script, example, ARIA fixture.</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/peteretelej/uiforagents/blob/main/SKILL.md"><code>SKILL.md</code></a> - the full adapter: workflow, variant API, token vocabulary.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The loop: read <code>llms.txt</code>, pick a component and variant, copy the item's files,
        wire tokens, then validate the render against the item's <code>fixture.aria.yml</code> with
        Playwright's ariaSnapshot.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="quickstart-col">
        <h2>For humans (and their agents)</h2>
        <p>Consume the kit through the per-project flow: install it, run one command to onboard, then keep a <code>uiforagents.json</code> config as the single source of truth for subset and direction:</p>
        <div class="uif-code-block">
          <div data-slot="header">
            <span data-slot="label">terminal</span>
            <button type="button" data-slot="copy">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre data-slot="code"><code>npm install uiforagents     # the kit + the uiforagents CLI
npx uiforagents init        # config + all components + tokens + docs
npx uiforagents tokens      # tokens.css from your direction
npx uiforagents add         # copy the configured subset
npx uiforagents scaffold    # design-system doc
npx uiforagents check       # adherence lint (reports, never fixes)</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>Prefer a checkout to a dependency? Point <code>kit</code> in the config at
        <code>../uiforagents</code> and run the same flow from the clone. This very site is
        the proof: an Astro static build where every page renders the copied items live.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
